# shadcn/ui Rules

## Responsibilities

- Standardize usage of shadcn/ui components as design system foundation
- Define when to use primitives vs compose custom components
- Keep shadcn components customizable via CSS variables, not forked unnecessarily

## Best Practices

- Install components via CLI: `npx shadcn@latest add [component]`
- Components live in `src/components/ui/` — treat as owned code, not node_modules
- Compose shadcn primitives into domain components in `components/` or `features/*/ui/`
- Use Radix UI accessibility built into shadcn components
- Extend variants via `cva` (class-variance-authority) in component file
- Form integration: shadcn Form + react-hook-form + Zod resolver

## Coding Standards

- Never modify shadcn component APIs without team agreement
- Wrap repeated patterns: `<FormField>` + `<Input>` → `<TextField>`
- Dialog for confirmations; Sheet for side panels/filters on mobile
- DropdownMenu for row actions; ContextMenu for power users
- DataTable built on `@tanstack/react-table` + shadcn Table

## Folder Structure

```
src/components/ui/          # shadcn primitives (button, input, dialog, etc.)
src/components/forms/       # Composed form fields
src/components/data-display/ # DataTable, etc.
```

## Naming Convention

- shadcn files: lowercase kebab-case (`dropdown-menu.tsx`)
- Composed components: PascalCase in parent folders
- Variants: semantic names (`default`, `destructive`, `outline`, `ghost`)

## Performance Rules

- Lazy-load Dialog/Sheet content when heavy
- Virtualize large Select option lists

## Security Rules

- AlertDialog required for irreversible actions (delete case, void invoice)

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Form with Zod + shadcn
<Form {...form}>
  <FormField control={form.control} name="title" render={({ field }) => (
    <FormItem>
      <FormLabel>Case Title</FormLabel>
      <FormControl><Input {...field} /></FormControl>
      <FormMessage />
    </FormItem>
  )} />
</Form>

// ✅ GOOD — Destructive confirmation
<AlertDialog>
  <AlertDialogAction onClick={handleDelete} className="bg-destructive">
    Delete Case
  </AlertDialogAction>
</AlertDialog>
```

## Things to Avoid

- Building custom modal/select when shadcn component exists
- Removing Radix accessibility attributes
- Inline styles overriding shadcn variants inconsistently
- Importing from `@radix-ui/*` directly in feature code (use shadcn wrapper)

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Using shadcn primitive where applicable
- [ ] Form fields have labels and error messages
- [ ] Destructive actions use AlertDialog
- [ ] Component variants use cva consistently
- [ ] Accessible (Radix handles most — verify focus trap in modals)
